ggml-metal: log + null-check ggml_metal_buffer_init result (iOS OOM safety)

Upstream's ggml_backend_metal_buffer_type_alloc_buffer uses the result of
ggml_metal_buffer_init without a NULL check. On iOS, a Metal OOM makes that
return NULL, and the following ggml_metal_buffer_is_shared(res) dereferences it
-> EXC_BAD_ACCESS (a hard crash) instead of a recoverable allocation failure.
Log the failure (matching ggml's GGML_LOG_ERROR convention) and return NULL so
the allocator surfaces a diagnosable error up the stack instead of crashing.

Applied at build time by ios/build-llama.sh to a build copy of the vendored
sources (the submodule stays pristine). Remove once upstreamed to ggml-org.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp
@@ -203,6 +203,11 @@
     ggml_metal_device_t ctx_dev = (ggml_metal_device_t)buft->device->context;
     ggml_metal_buffer_t res = ggml_metal_buffer_init(ctx_dev, size, shared);

+    if (res == NULL) {
+        GGML_LOG_ERROR("%s: error: failed to allocate Metal buffer of %zu bytes (out of memory)\n", __func__, size);
+        return NULL;
+    }
+
     ggml_backend_buffer_i buf_i = ggml_metal_buffer_is_shared(res)
         ? ggml_backend_metal_buffer_shared_i
         : ggml_backend_metal_buffer_private_i;
